<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basilica of Bom Jesus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Basilica of Bom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> church in Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, completed in 1605 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> style. It holds the tomb and remains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-xavier">Saint Francis Xavier</a>, which are displayed to pilgrims at intervals. With the other churches and convents of Old Goa, the former capital of Portuguese India, it was declared a World Heritage Site in 1986.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basilica-of-bom-jesus.jpg" alt="Basilica of Bom Jesus" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: iMahesh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_Elevation_of_Basilica_of_Bom_Jesus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
